# MMAI published-site settings. NON-SECRET: values here are settings and the NAMES of environment variables, never keys or
# passwords. Loaded at start-up (server/__init__.py) only for variables that the host has not already set, so anything passed
# on the run command or injected by the hosting platform wins.
#
# AI with the user's own Anthropic key (publish credential proxy): put the credential's website_url_env_var and
# website_token_env_var NAMES here. Left blank (and with no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY on the host) the AI step has no credentials and
# FAILS CLOSED: groups are held with the "No AI credentials" reason and nothing is marked ready - there is no rules-only fallback.
MMAI_AI_URL_VAR=
MMAI_AI_TOKEN_VAR=
# All AI calls use the single approved runtime model, including country reads.
MMAI_AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
MMAI_AI_FAST_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
MMAI_SCHEDULER_DATASETS=real,test
MMAI_TRUST_VISITOR_ID=0

# --- Production hosting (T17, DigitalOcean): these are set as real environment variables in the App Platform spec (.do/app.yaml),
# never here. Listed for reference only:
#   DATABASE_URL            postgresql://... (managed Postgres). Unset = SQLite file (MMAI_DB), as in the preview.
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY       MateBot AI's own Anthropic key (secret). With no ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL the app talks to Anthropic directly.
#   MMAI_AI_MODE            own-key | sandbox (optional override of the automatic choice)
#   MMAI_PUBLIC_BASE_URL    https://app.matebot.com.au  (address printed into resume / Bring a mate / emailed-form links)
#   MMAI_FRAME_ANCESTORS    'self' https://www.apartmentlivingmelbourne.com.au https://apartmentlivingmelbourne.com.au
